---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import DayRating from '../../rateDay/rateDay.astro'
export const post = {
  day: 1,
  title: 'My first blog post',
  date: '2026-09-06',
  description: "Why I started this blog and what I'll upload here.",
  category: 'Daily',
  tags: ['Astro', 'Tailwind CSS', 'Web Development'],
}
---

<Layout>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-24 pt-32">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-16">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm">
        <span
          class="font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--secondary)]"
        >
          {post.category}
        </span>

        <span class="text-[var(--border)]">/</span>

        <span class="text-[var(--muted)]">
          Day {post.day}
        </span>
      </div>

      <h1
        class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
      >
        {post.title}
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">
        {
          new Date(post.date).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
            day: 'numeric',
            month: 'long',
            year: 'numeric',
          })
        }
      </p>

      <p
        class="mt-8 border-l-2 border-[var(--secondary)] pl-5 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--muted)] sm:text-xl"
      >
        {post.description}
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="space-y-14 leading-8">
      <!-- Section -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          Why did I start?
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[var(--secondary)]"
              ></span>

              <span>
                I wanna use this blog as a place to share my thoughts and what
                I'm currently working on.
              </span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[var(--secondary)]"
              ></span>

              <span> I wanna remember what I did every day. </span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[var(--secondary)]"
              ></span>

              <span> I wanna practice my English every day. </span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[var(--secondary)]"
              ></span>

              <span>
                I'm hoping it will help me stay motivated to improve myself
                every day.
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Meybe It will also help my readers to learn something new, or at
            least give them some inspiration. <br />
            Or maybe it will be that interesting that they'll read this for fun.
          </p>
          <p>
            Who knows? I don't know yet, but I hope it will be a good experience
            for both me and my readers.<br />
            <span class="text-gray-400 text-[15px]"
              >(I'd try to add imgs to my posts, but I'm not a person which
              likes to take photos, so let's see how it'll go.)</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          What will be uploaded here?
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <p>
            It's kinda hard to say, I think it will be short description of what
            I did that day,<br />
            what I learned, how i learned it, and I will try to explain it in a easy
            way <br />
            so my readers can understand it too. <br />
            I'll also write about my plans for the next day, and I'll check if I achieved
            plans I set. <br />
            At the end I will review that whole day and rate it from 1 to 10, and
            write what I could do better. <br />
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          Day 1
        </h2>

        <p>
          Today, I got to the point, where i can finnaly write day 1. I decided
          to create this blog probably 2 or 3 days ago, and becouse I spent most
          of my time in work I couldn't start it earlier. this whole blog is
          wrotten in Astro, and It's my first time using it. I decide to use
          this freamwork becouse It should be fast even with many posts,
          definetly faster than React that I use most of the time, it has
          similar logic to React, so It wasn't hard to learn, If u want to learn
          Astro, u should start with HTML and Javascript, becouse It's
          combination of those two, after that, u can just try it just create
          [FileName].astro and write code like this:
          <pre
            class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-6 text-sm leading-7"><code>---<br />JavaScript here<br />---<br /><br />HTML here</code></pre>
          Besides that, I recently started listning a new podcast named "Luke's English
          Podcast", Meybe its not not the best podcast ever,it contains weird topics,
          like Vampires, I still dont believe he was talking 45 minutes about Vampires,
          and what they can represent, but becouse topics are different every time,
          It's not boring, and only 992ep left me to listen, I also listned 3 audiobooks
          recently(not today), becouse my work is boring, and I have to listen to
          something.
          <ul>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[var(--secondary)]"
              ></span>

              <span>
                "The Upside of Stress" - McGonigal Kelly, It was quite good
                book, it was about stress, most of people think that stress is a
                bad thing, but not in this book, author is thinking that the way
                we are thinking about the stress is the reason, why its bad, if
                we'll think about stress like a good thing that help us when we
                do somethimg that is important for us then stress should become
                our ally
              </span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[var(--secondary)]"
              ></span>

              <span>
                "Emotional intelligence"-Daniel Goleman,I'm not a big fan of
                this book, It lasted forever (about 20h) , I even thought about
                turn this audiobook off, but I didn't , so it was about this
                that emotional intelligence is the most important thing, u need
                to achieve a success, I'm still not fully agree with this, but
                It can be helpful when u have empathy and u can understand what
                other people feel, and control your emotions and u can even work
                to build Emotional intelligence so why not?
              </span>
            </li>

            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[var(--secondary)]"
              ></span>

              <span>
                "Mindfulness in 10 minutes"- S.J. Scott and Barrie Davenport,
                this audiobook was quick and fun to listen, it was about 71
                habits that'll help you to live in present moment, I didn't
                expect a lot from this audiobook, but it has some rly good
                habits, they aren't hard and some of them are just better
                version of things we are doing every day, the most important
                thing for me I needed to relise was that if u will wake up at 7
                a.m. and other person will go to sleep at the same time and wake
                up at 5 a.m. and it'll be repeating for 40 years, so the person
                that wake up later, lost almost 5 full years (if 1d = 17h (2h
                lost per day )):
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          Calculations:
          <pre
            class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-6 text-sm leading-7"><code>P1(0-5AM) 5H SPLEEP
AVAILABLE TIME: (24-5) x 365 x 40 = 277'400 H

P2(0-7AM) 7H SPLEEP
AVAILABLE TIME: (24-7) x 365 x 40 = 248'200 H

DIFFRENCE: 277'400 - 248'200 = 29'200 H / (24-7) H ~ 1'718 D / 365 D ~ 4.7 Y
            </code></pre>
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          Plans for tomorrow
        </h2>

        <p>
          I'll wake up early,I'll make my bed, I'll drink glass of water, I will create blog page and about (now it doesn't exits only day page, and home)
          I also want to read book titled "think faster, talk smarter" unfortunetly it's not translated to polish so it'll be challanging, at least I want to start this book,
          Thats probably everything, I'd be really satisfied if I'll do everything
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          How I rate this day
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <p>
            I'll give 7/10, it was quite productive day (I hope this blog is readable, I know, I'm not very good at writing)
          </p>
        </div>
        
      </section>
      <DayRating class="w-full" rating={7}></DayRating>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
